# recv returns [Result.Ok v] on successful receive from a oneshot channel
# Phase 3: recv protocol redesign (T-811)
#
# Sends 99 to a oneshot sender, then receives on the oneshot receiver.
# Exercises the [Result.Ok v] success path of builtin_recv for OneshotReceiver.
# The [Closed] path for oneshot (receiver used after value consumed) is
# tracked in B-228; it requires expressing sender-drop in tinct.
[
  chans: [oneshot-channel]
  rx: [head chans]
  tx: [head [tail chans]]
  sent: [send tx 99]
  first-result: [if [= sent []] [recv rx] [recv rx]]
]
[match %.first-result
  [Result.Ok v]: v
  [Closed]: -1]
=== error
[E001] key not found: first-result (defined at 1:1-1:1) (accessed at 14:8-14:22)
  in accessing .first-result at 14:8-14:22

=== warn
[UndefinedVariable] undefined variable: v
